1785864295951426	edict-dev	itc:v3:AWLkkmTOfzk5kQAAAAAAQeqtbv7rtAAAAAEvJg		item.create	bn-1z2g	{"description":"The responder's SKIP_LABELS list (src/commands/responder.rs) misses several labels used purely for status/coordination announcements: task-update (bone state transitions, e.g. 'bn-1234 -> doing'), coord:handoff (worker handoff, sibling of already-skipped coord:interface/coord:blocker/coord:merge), triage-reply (responder's own ack format, sibling of spawn-ack), and task-blocked (already-tracked blocked-work alert, sibling of task-done/agent-error). Because worker agents get random names (via rite generate-name) rather than a project-prefixed name, these messages aren't caught by the project-agent skip check either, so they fall through to handle_triage's haiku classifier, which misreads status prose like 'fixing the bug in X' as a new work request and files a duplicate bone + spawns dev-loop. Add these four labels to SKIP_LABELS.","kind":"bug","title":"responder: skip status/coordination labels from triage"}	blake3:6F-kRwQGhvP3VRiqHoxGbjtqn2yExmuPO6bZgOFsOe8
