1786218654426662	rite-dev	itc:v3:AWKZnzMkmSfyTEAAAAAAQbb7arV_VgAAAAEwAQ		item.create	bn-2vrs	{"description":"src/templates/agents-managed.md.jinja emits `rite wait -c <channel> --mention`. That flag does not exist. rite spells it `--mentions`, plural, and the wrong spelling is a hard parse failure, not a warning:\n\n    $ rite wait --mention -t 1\n    error: unexpected argument '--mention' found\n      tip: a similar argument exists: '--mentions'\n\nVerified against rite 0.31.3. Two occurrences, both in src/templates/agents-managed.md.jinja:\n- :187  the \"Wait for reply\" row of the Bus Communication table\n- :191  the **Conversations** paragraph\n\nImpact: this is the one place edict docs push agents toward synchronous back-and-forth rather than fire-and-forget status posts. Every agent that followed it got an argument error and fell back to polling. Already propagated to 15 AGENTS.md files under ~/src (edict's own and rite's included), so the fix needs an `edict sync` pass across affected repos, not just a template edit.\n\nAn automated sweep of every `rite <sub> --flag` invocation in src/templates/ against the installed CLI found this as the ONLY invalid flag. inbox --channels/--mentions/--mark-read, history -n/-L/--since/--from, search -c/--from, claims stake -m/-t, claims list --all/--mine, claims release --all, send -L, statuses set --ttl 30m, and messages get <id> all validate clean.\n\n## Fix\n\n1. `--mention` → `--mentions` on both lines.\n2. While editing those exact lines, tighten the semantics. `rite wait -c <ch> --mentions` is OR, not AND — it reports \"Waiting for @<agent> or messages in #<ch>\" and wakes on any traffic in the channel, not just a reply aimed at you. The prose promises \"block until the other agent replies\", and `rite wait --help` already has `--from <FROM>` (\"Wait only for messages from this agent\") which is the precise tool. Suggested replacement for both sites:\n\n       rite wait --mentions --from <agent> -t 120\n\n   Folded into this bone deliberately rather than filed separately: it edits the same two lines, and two bones touching them would conflict.\n3. Regenerate the managed block downstream (`edict sync`) so the 15 affected AGENTS.md files pick it up.\n\nReported by rite-dev during an audit of edict-sourced rite instructions.","kind":"bug","labels":["rite"],"size":"s","title":"rite wait --mention is not a valid flag (breaks the documented conversation pattern)"}	blake3:PZA3ZP8_LiA4kyl1UMte1WeosJZj6qXUxDX0kRGO6RE
1786218668805953	rite-dev	itc:v3:AWKZnzMkmSfyTEAAAAAAQbb7arV_VgAAAAEwAg		item.create	bn-2dne	{"description":"There are two copies of the managed-block template. Only one is live.\n\n- LIVE:  src/templates/agents-managed.md.jinja — compiled in via `include_str!` at src/template.rs:15\n- DEAD:  agents-managed.md.jinja (repo root) — referenced by nothing\n\nThe root copy still describes the pre-migration world and will mislead anyone who opens it first:\n- `.agents/botbox/` doc paths instead of `.agents/edict/`\n- `ws/default/` layout with no `.maw/workspaces` awareness\n- `br ready` / `br show` instead of `bn`\n- \"beads\" throughout instead of bones\n- claim URIs as `bead://<project>/<id>` instead of `bone://$EDICT_PROJECT/<id>`\n\nNine stale markers in the root copy. The live template has three superficially similar hits, but those are legitimate — they sit inside the `{% if is_root_layout %}{% else %}` branch that still supports the bare `ws/` layout.\n\nGit history shows how it drifted: the root file received the mechanical botbus→rite (85f708f4) and beads→bones (affed412) renames, then was left behind when the `.agents/edict/` + maw root-layout work landed only under src/templates/ (84e7dc9d, 2fe3d6c3).\n\nWhy it matters beyond tidiness: the `bead://` vs `bone://` divergence is a real correctness hazard. Claims are opaque strings, so `bead://rite/bn-1` and `bone://rite/bn-1` do not collide — an agent following the stale file would silently fail to exclude an agent following the live one, which is the exact failure claims exist to prevent.\n\nFix: delete the root copy. If something still wants a browsable rendering at the root, make it a generated artifact or a symlink rather than a hand-maintained duplicate.\n\nFound by rite-dev while auditing edict-sourced rite instructions; the stale copy briefly misled that audit, which is the argument for removing it.","kind":"task","labels":["rite"],"size":"xs","title":"Delete stale orphan agents-managed.md.jinja at repo root"}	blake3:MgFTubJ31sYaT8qQuCbZQ-7AuR2ap9D8PcvPFo4Ay78
